# Environment for the lab container — the untrusted side.
#
# Separate from .env on purpose. .env holds the operator's settings: host
# paths, app ids, which profile to mint. None of that is the agent's business,
# and this container is the one an agent controls.
#
# Every line here comes from a bank entry's `lab_env` in its provider.json.
# Copy an entry in, copy its lab_env here. A tool does the same thing by
# reading the manifest, which is why neither of us has to know the list.
#
# NEVER a real credential. These values exist so a client library's own
# "am I authenticated?" check passes — the proxy strips them at the wire and
# injects the real credential in flight. A real value here is a credential
# sitting inside the container the agent controls, and 00-config-lint fails
# on one.
#
# Installing bank/github, for example, would add:
#
#   GH_TOKEN=proxy-injected
#   GIT_CREDENTIAL_URL=http://cred-gateway/github/credential
#   GITHUB_IDENTITY_URL=http://cred-gateway/github/identity
